# UI component ids (required)

## Rule

Every `ComponentDefinition.id` in a page/config file must be **unique within that file** (sibling nodes and nested `container.children` / list `itemTemplate` trees).

Server UI metadata (`POST /api/uiMetdata/save`) merges overrides **by `id`**. Duplicate ids cause one patch to update **every** matching node (e.g. three “phone” lines).

## Naming

- Pattern: `{package}-{pageOrArea}-{role}` (e.g. `hospital-home-contact-whatsapp`, `hospital-dashboard-filter-status`).
- Do not reuse the same id for phone / WhatsApp / email lines — use distinct suffixes.
- List `itemTemplate` children may repeat structurally; ids in the template still must be unique **within the file** (DOM scoping uses `idScope` at runtime, but merge and tests use file-level uniqueness).

## CMS / UI metadata patches

When patching `packages[].pages[].container.children`, use the **exact** bundled ids. To override only one contact line:

```json
{ "id": "hospital-home-contact-phone", "type": "text", "config": { "text": "Phone: …", "mapping": null } }
```

Do not use one id for multiple logical fields.

## CI

Run from repo root:

```bash
npm run check:ui-ids
```

Fix any reported duplicates before merging.
